Type: Package
Package: occPlus
Title: Fitting occupancy models for eDNA reads data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alex", "Diana", , "ad23269@essex.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Luveen", "Wadhwani", , "luveen.w@columbia.edu", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Implements a multi-species occupancy model for environmental
    DNA (eDNA) read-count data, following the statistical framework of
    Griffin et al.  (2020) <doi:10.1111/rssc.12390>. The model explicitly
    accounts for false positive and false negative observation errors at
    both the field sampling stage and the laboratory amplification stage
    of eDNA surveys.  Species co-occurrence patterns are captured through
    a latent factor model, enabling concurrent ordination alongside
    occupancy estimation. Model parameters are inferred via Bayesian
    methods, using either a Stan-based Hamiltonian Monte Carlo sampler or
    a custom Gibbs MCMC backend. Functions are provided for model fitting,
    posterior summarisation, and visualisation of occupancy probabilities,
    detection rates, covariate effects, and inter-species correlation
    matrices.
